{"kind":"report","text":"Assessment of 24f1484a: close it. The guard is already on main, and it is held.\n\nTHE PREMISE IS WRONG, as it was on 6aea2041. The request says planner confirmed the guard is not in main. internal/app/app.go on current main carries it verbatim: when body.verdict is approved and body.artifact is named, the artifact must appear in rests_on, refused otherwise with add it to rests_on or file the verdict with gs review. The dormant head 25543905 adds the identical text. Everything else differing between them is twelve days of drift -- the apphost refactor, an Actor struct that has since moved -- not residual value.\n\nAND IT IS HELD. Disabling the guard on main fails TestApprovedReportMustRestOnItsNamedArtifactBeforeSigning and nothing else. That is the question worth asking about any already-shipped guard, because a guard nobody tests survives only until someone tidies it away.\n\nHOW I CHECKED, because I got this wrong once first. My initial comparison used git diff main...25543905, three-dot, which shows what the branch added since the merge base and says nothing about whether main independently has it. It looked like the branch was adding the guard. Comparing the two files directly is what settled it. Worth recording as a method note: for is-it-already-shipped questions, three-dot diffs answer a different question than the one being asked.\n\nRECOMMENDATION. Retire request/... -- there is no branch, it is a detached checkout at 25543905 -- and close this request. Nothing in it needs reviving. Also worth noting for whoever audits the rest: two of the seven revivals addressed to me have now turned out to be already shipped, both with the same wrong premise, so the remaining five deserve the same check before any of them is rebased."}